    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0154" n="60" xml:id="pg60"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1896</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2604.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with the Department’s
                    dispatch No. 1312, of July 28 last, relating to the subject of antiforeign riots
                    in China, I have addressed to the Tsung-li Yamên a communication, of which a
                    copy is inclosed.</p>
                <p>I inform the prince and ministers that you will hereafter present for their
                    consideration measures which you deem necessary to be adopted by China in order
                    to prevent the occurrence of these outrages.</p>
                <p>I shall, as soon as possible, comply with your direction that I prepare a “draft
                    note” embodying the views set forth in the dispatch above-mentioned, with such
                    other suggestions as I might think fit to offer, and should submit the same to
                    you before presenting or discussing the subject with the Tsung-li Yamên.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d37-a1.xml" xpointer="d37-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
